From: Whisky Runtime CI <runtime@whisky.local>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: Initialize D3D11On12CreateDevice outputs

D3D11On12CreateDevice is not implemented by Wine or D3DMetal. Keep the
failure explicit instead of returning an unrelated D3D11 device, but honor
the COM output contract by clearing every caller-provided output before
returning E_NOTIMPL.

This prevents callers that inspect or clean up outputs after failure from
using stale pointers or a stale feature level.

---
 dlls/d3d11/d3d11_main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/d3d11/d3d11_main.c b/dlls/d3d11/d3d11_main.c
index 75986318..989c023e 100644
--- a/dlls/d3d11/d3d11_main.c
+++ b/dlls/d3d11/d3d11_main.c
@@ -390,5 +390,12 @@ HRESULT WINAPI D3D11On12CreateDevice(IUnknown *device, UINT flags,
             device, flags, feature_levels, feature_level_count, queues, queue_count,
             node_mask, d3d11_device, d3d11_immediate_context, obtained_feature_level);
 
+    if (d3d11_device)
+        *d3d11_device = NULL;
+    if (d3d11_immediate_context)
+        *d3d11_immediate_context = NULL;
+    if (obtained_feature_level)
+        *obtained_feature_level = 0;
+
     return E_NOTIMPL;
 }
-- 
